+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Physical MAIN authorization plus engagement or active lateral control and target/actual speeds of at least 30 km/h must persist for 0.5 seconds before SET−. A valid gas release requests SET on the next available sample without an extra confirmation dwell. A request gap at release is retained for at most 0.1s and recovery requests SET without an extra confirmation dwell. Actual stock engagement synchronizes MAIN tracking without restoring revoked authorization.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+After turning ON, restart and physically operate MAIN. Initial MAIN parity follows AutoEngage but never authorizes SET by itself. After brake or CANCEL, retain MAIN standby and rearm only on a fresh gas press/release at 30 km/h or above. MAIN OFF prevents automatic starts.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Below 30 km/h actual speed, the driver must accelerate. Startup SET is bounded to six frames/120ms and releases on stock ON. Missing feedback alternates 0/10ms retry slots; only stock-ON-confirmed timing is remembered. The confirmed startup slot also carries into speed matching; each unanswered speed request changes its next slot without shortening quiet periods. No direct braking or standstill launch; vehicle acceptance remains unvalidated.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
